WEBVTT

00:01.170 --> 00:02.450
Ahem!

00:03.320 --> 00:05.980
In Japan, when the rainy season comes,

00:06.460 --> 00:09.780
and everything's all damp and gloomy,

00:09.780 --> 00:14.890
a moment's rest can lead to a tenacious black mold infestation!

00:14.890 --> 00:18.450
Normal bathrooms like this are particularly humid,

00:18.450 --> 00:20.560
making them primo spots for mold hotbeds!

00:20.560 --> 00:23.610
It's our duty to take this challenge head on,

00:23.610 --> 00:27.460
and clean this place 'til it shines!

00:27.460 --> 00:30.720
Hey, can you guys listen for once?

00:31.550 --> 00:34.340
Boasting wastes time. I've no use for it.

00:34.340 --> 00:37.720
We've got to finish cleaning before Master's bathtime.

00:39.360 --> 00:41.220
I'm back!

00:41.520 --> 00:45.480
This vinegar will take down the really clingy mold!

00:45.780 --> 00:48.480
Just a piece of grandmotherly wisd—uaah!

00:56.200 --> 00:58.200
What're ya doin', Lene?

00:59.630 --> 01:02.180
I-I'm so sorry...

01:04.190 --> 01:05.660
What happened, girls?

01:05.660 --> 01:06.830
Are you all right?

01:07.420 --> 01:10.340
Oh, you're so clumsy, Lene.

01:22.540 --> 01:24.180
That's cold, Lene!

01:24.180 --> 01:27.610
Master's always letting you off with the "you're so clumsy" shtick!

01:28.150 --> 01:30.610
When you mixed detergent into Master's ramen,

01:30.610 --> 01:33.610
when you blew up an egg in the microwave,

01:33.610 --> 01:38.740
when you got sucked into the vacuum cleaner and got all the dust we'd just cleaned everywhere,

01:38.740 --> 01:40.230
every <i>single</i> time,

01:40.230 --> 01:42.750
Master just called you clumsy and laughed it off!

01:43.190 --> 01:47.120
Meanwhile, I'm workin' my screw holes off, and I get jack in return!

01:47.710 --> 01:50.430
Maybe it seems that way...

01:50.430 --> 01:52.810
but I'm giving it my all, too.

01:53.920 --> 01:57.280
If you were giving it your all, everything'd be just peachy!

01:57.280 --> 01:59.390
Honestly, you just get in the way.

02:01.040 --> 02:03.520
You don't have to say it like that...

02:04.520 --> 02:08.250
H-Hey, let's stop fighting and make up!

02:08.250 --> 02:09.520
You're sisters, so...

02:09.800 --> 02:12.090
We're just configured that way!

02:12.090 --> 02:13.990
It's not like we're real sisters.

02:19.450 --> 02:21.880
It shines

02:21.880 --> 02:25.940
My singing voice is endless

02:25.940 --> 02:32.520
My eternal pledge is only for you

02:32.520 --> 02:39.260
I wonder if you're your usual self

02:39.260 --> 02:44.740
I'll sparkle with you

02:44.740 --> 02:47.750
Install dream

02:52.640 --> 02:57.630
The arms of the clock advance

02:58.860 --> 03:04.050
and with them so does time

03:04.050 --> 03:11.210
When you are sad, I open my tiny arms

03:11.210 --> 03:17.560
and embrace you

03:19.570 --> 03:21.870
Fly

03:21.870 --> 03:26.160
My singing voice is tender

03:26.160 --> 03:32.540
I can remember your shape

03:32.540 --> 03:35.540
and that wasn't brought about by a program

03:35.540 --> 03:39.150
Let us experience

03:39.150 --> 03:44.840
the turmoil in my heart together

03:44.840 --> 03:47.910
Install dream

03:48.830 --> 03:52.330
It's a Race! One Lap Around the Park!

03:48.830 --> 03:52.330
It's a Race! One Lap Around the Park!

03:48.830 --> 03:52.330
It's a Race! One Lap Around the Park!

03:52.740 --> 03:55.730
Once we're out of the rainy season, we'll be close to summer vacation.

03:56.800 --> 03:59.600
It's summer, so we should go to the beach!

03:59.600 --> 04:01.450
I would prefer the mountains.

04:01.450 --> 04:04.770
I have long been interested in guerrilla warfare.

04:04.770 --> 04:07.310
Is that a summer thing where you're from?

04:08.770 --> 04:11.810
No matter where we go, it'll cost money.

04:12.130 --> 04:14.410
I'll just have to keep working and saving.

04:18.000 --> 04:20.470
Are you still fighting?

04:20.470 --> 04:22.680
You can always make up...

04:26.350 --> 04:28.110
Whatcha lookin' at all alone?

04:29.020 --> 04:31.580
N-Nothing at all!

04:42.950 --> 04:44.970
Hm? What're you doing?

04:45.310 --> 04:48.470
You don't want to sleep next to me that much?

04:48.820 --> 04:50.400
I-It's not that!

04:50.400 --> 04:52.920
I'll be waking up early tomorrow,

04:52.920 --> 04:55.360
so I don't want to disturb you when I do.

04:56.060 --> 04:57.860
What are you waking up early for?

04:58.870 --> 05:00.740
Um, well...

05:01.800 --> 05:03.610
Good night!

05:19.860 --> 05:20.930
Suspicious.

05:20.930 --> 05:23.000
She's definitely up to something.

05:56.790 --> 05:58.250
